   "daf": "40a",
   "sentenceId": 17,
   "he": "רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר וְכוּ׳. אָמַר עוּלָּא: הֲלָכָה כְּרַבִּי יְהוּדָה. וְכֵן אָמַר רַבִּי יִצְחָק נַפָּחָא: הֲלָכָה כְּרַבִּי יְהוּדָה.",
   "en": "§ The mishna continues by citing an opposing opinion. «Rabbi Yehuda says:» In either case, whether he consummated levirate marriage or performed ḥalitza, if there is a father who is still alive, the property belongs to the father. The Gemara cites a ruling on this dispute: «Ulla said:» The «halakha is in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Yehuda. And similarly, Rabbi Yitzḥak Nappaḥa said: The halakha is in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Yehuda.»"
  }
 ],
